nRelated programs\nFaculties & departments\nMechanical Engineering at University of Victoria is known for its innovative research and excellent academic programs.\nIn mechanical engineering, you\u2019ll work on cutting edge technology and systems. As a mechanical engineer, you'll use your problem-solving and teamwork skills to work on real-world problems. You will see the results of your efforts and have a chance to make an impact on society.\nDegree programs offered\nAerospace Systems Engineering (MEng)\nBiomedical Systems (MEng)\nMechanical Engineering (MASc)\nMechanical Engineering (MEng)\nMechanical Engineering (PhD)\nProgram\nExpected length\nProject or thesis\nCourse-based\nASE MEng\n1 year\nNo\nYes\nBISY MEng\n12-16 months\nNo\nYes\nMEng, MASc\n2 years\nYes\nNo\nPhD\n3 years\nYes\nNo\nQuick facts\nProgram options:\nMasters, Doctorate\nProgram delivery:\nOn-campus\nDynamic learning:\nCo-op optional\nAreas of focus\nAdvanced manufacturing\nAdvanced materials\nAeronautics and aerospace\nBiomedical engineering\nComputational and continuum mechanics\nComputational design and computer aided engineering\nAlternate energy technologies and systems\nIndustrial sensing and optics\nMechatronics and controls\nMicro-electromechanical systems\nOcean engineering and ocean energy\nRobotics and mechanisms\nFaculties and departments\nFaculty of Engineering and Computer Science\nMechanical Engineering\nNeed help?\nContact the applicable graduate secretary:\nMechanical Engineering\nAlison Ward at\nmech.grad@uvic.ca.\nBiomedical Systems\nHector Lopez Segarra at\nbisy_meng@uvic.ca.\nAerospace Systems\nHector Lopez Segarra at\nase_meng@uvic.ca.\n< Explore more programs\nFavourite this program\n0 saved\n\u200b UVic Instagram \u200b UVic Facebook \u200b UVic Twitter \u200b UVic Linkedin \u200b UVic YouTube View all UVic social media\nQuicklinks\nAbout UVic\nAdmissions\nResearch\nNews & media\nEvents\nCareers\nDonate\nInfo for...\nStudents\nFaculty & staff\nAlumni\nIndigenous\nInternat